  "scoring_key_verified": true,
  "notes": "Optional instrument. Screener result; clinical evaluation required. Sum scoring, total 0–72; cutoff 21 per Foa et al. 2002 (as cited in PMC4530108, which notes later recommendations from 14 to 36). Subscale membership (hoarding 1, 7, 13; checking 2, 8, 14; ordering 3, 9, 15; neutralizing 4, 10, 16; washing 5, 11, 17; obsessing 6, 12, 18) matches the item content on the form.",
  "instructions": "The following statements refer to experiences that many people have in their everyday lives. Circle the number that best describes HOW MUCH that experience has DISTRESSED or BOTHERED you during the PAST MONTH.",
  "source_url": "https://pcl.psychiatry.uw.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/OCI-R-Scale-and-Manual.pdf",
  "text_source": "OCI-R form ('Copyright by Edna B. Foa 2002') as reproduced by the University of Washington Psychiatry Consultation Line, transcribed verbatim 2026-09-16 (line-wrapped items joined). The same document's scoring page suggests a total of 18 or more and reports subscale means; this app keeps the sum scoring and the cutoff of 21 from Foa et al. 2002.",
